{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 23,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When you sit down to dine with a ruler, consider carefully what is set before you,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "and put a knife to your throat if you possess a great appetite.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not crave his delicacies, for that food is deceptive.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not wear yourself out to get rich; be wise enough to restrain yourself.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When you glance at wealth, it disappears, for it makes wings for itself and flies like an eagle to the sky.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not eat the bread of a stingy man, and do not crave his delicacies;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "for he is keeping track, inwardly counting the cost. “Eat and drink,” he says to you, but his heart is not with you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You will vomit up what little you have eaten and waste your pleasant words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not speak to a fool, for he will despise the wisdom of your words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not move an ancient boundary stone or encroach on the fields of the fatherless,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "for their Redeemer is strong; He will take up their case against you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Apply your heart to instruction and your ears to words of knowledge.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not withhold discipline from a child; although you strike him with a rod, he will not die.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Strike him with a rod, and you will deliver his soul from Sheol.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My son, if your heart is wise, my own heart will indeed rejoice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My inmost being will rejoice when your lips speak what is right.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not let your heart envy sinners, but always continue in the fear of the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For surely there is a future, and your hope will not be cut off.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Listen, my son, and be wise, and guide your heart on the right course.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not join those who drink too much wine or gorge themselves on meat.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the drunkard and the glutton will come to poverty, and drowsiness will clothe them in rags.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Listen to your father who gave you life, and do not despise your mother when she is old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Invest in truth and never sell it— in wisdom and instruction and understanding.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The father of a righteous man will greatly rejoice, and he who fathers a wise son will delight in him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May your father and mother be glad, and may she who gave you birth rejoice!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My son, give me your heart, and let your eyes delight in my ways.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For a prostitute is a deep pit, and an adulteress is a narrow well.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Like a robber she lies in wait and multiplies the faithless among men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who has woe? Who has sorrow? Who has contentions? Who has complaints? Who has needless wounds? Who has bloodshot eyes?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Those who linger over wine, who go to taste mixed drinks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not gaze at wine while it is red, when it sparkles in the cup and goes down smoothly.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the end it bites like a snake and stings like a viper.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Your eyes will see strange things, and your mind will utter perversities.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You will be like one sleeping on the high seas or lying on the top of a mast:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.23.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.23.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "“They struck me, but I feel no pain! They beat me, but I did not know it! When can I wake up to search for another drink?”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
